  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "The critical fractional Sobolev embedding remains noncompact even in the radial space, and the prescribed mass constraint can be lost by a weak Palais-Smale limit. The authors develop the mass-preserving fiber geometry and Pohozaev constraint for the Kirchhoff and nonlocal Poisson terms, obtain a minimax sequence with an additional vanishing Pohozaev condition, and derive a critical energy bound excluding critical concentration. Their local estimates force a negative limiting Lagrange multiplier and recover the full mass with strong convergence, which is substantially beyond a routine variational existence proof.",
